A||||4||DJRice||Possible TCC Lockup Solenoid problems?||||1||
Z||000000||DJRice||11-28-2000||04:59 PM||||I have an 86 Auto 4 cyl (188K) that occasionally likes to stall out when going from Park to Reverse.  It also seems to hang a bit going from 2-3.  <P>I am thinking the TCC lockup solenoid.  <BR>Is there anything else I should check?<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-28-2000||08:23 PM||||May be just a tired transmission with 188K miles needing a rebuild. When my TCC went the car would not get out of 3rd gear.  When I've had autos delay upshifting, the transmission needed an overhaul.  Check the level of the fluid, should be red, no burnt smell.||||reg||3
Z||000002||afRaceR||11-28-2000||10:12 PM||||The stalling when you put it in gear sounds like a TCC, but since it only happens ocasionally its more likely a sticky valve or solenoid. And the hangy 2-3 shift definately sounds like a hangy valve. <BR>Usually, when there's that much trash in a transmission, its shot. But sometimes you can change the fluid and filter and it works great. Also, get a product called Trans-X and add that to the fluid. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||11-29-2000||02:27 AM||||Ive got the same problem, and maybe there's something to that tired tranny thing.  I've already replaced fluid and filter, and the solenoid, and it didnt help.  As a matter of fact, as part of my V-6 rebuild, I replaced every darned sensor in the machine.<P>Ive noticed that if I pop it into drive...it'll stall...but if i slowly slide it into drive...it wont.  It'll also stall when I pop it into park after pulling into the garage.  Again...going slowly into park wont do it.  Ive given up trying to fix it and adjusted my shifting habits instead.||||reg||1
Z||000004||afRaceR||11-29-2000||02:47 AM||||If you ever get really bored and have some time on your hand, get a manual for a 125C transmission and pull the valve body. Check and make sure all the valves move nice and free. Dirt and trash can make valves kind of sticky sometimes and the only way to completely clean the VB is by pulling the valves out. Just go slow and pull one valve out at a time.||||reg||1
